How to install in Lyon
======================

The dependencies are already compiled and installed at Lyon, so the process to compile and use it is

  for i in /sps/km3net/users/hugon/sw/env/*sh; do source $i; done
  cd [your checkout path]/trunk
  mkdir build
  cd build
  cmake .. -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=g++-510 -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=gcc-510 [-D__NEW_TESTING_ALGO__=d] [-DFULL_OPTIMIZATION=1]
  make [-j5]

The parameters between [] are optional, they are useful to use the last features (for which the test were not yet fully done) and all the compilation optimization (longer compilation but faster running)

How to install elsewhere
========================
you need: gcc >= 4.7, cmake > 3.0.0, libconfig++, geant4.10 and root5.34
always needed:
  source [your checkout path]/trunk/resources/geant.sh

Best case:
you can install at least gcc and libconfig directly in your system (debian wheezy)

  cd [your checkout path]/trunk
  mkdir build
  cd build
  cmake .. [-D__NEW_TESTING_ALGO__=d] [-DFULL_OPTIMIZATION=1]
  make [-j5]

Other case:
- you have to specify the path of libconfig++:
  export LIBCONFIG_ROOT=[the path to your libconfig++ installation]
  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$LIBCONFIG_ROOT/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
  export CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH=/sps/km3net/users/hugon/sw/libconfig-1.5/include/
then normal compilation

- you have to specify the path of gcc:
  ln -s [gcc install]/bin/gcc [gcc install]/bin/gcc-[your gcc version]
  ln -s [gcc install]/bin/g++ [gcc install]/bin/g++-[your gcc version]
  cd [...]/build
  cmake .. -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=g++-[your gcc version] -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=gcc-[your gcc version] [-D__NEW_TESTING_ALGO__=d] [-DFULL_OPTIMIZATION=1]

be sure that  [gcc install]/bin is in your PATH environment variable and  [gcc install]/lib:[gcc install]/lib64 in your LD_LIBRARY_PATH environement variable.

Documentation 
========================
The doxygen documentation is provided in the folder documentation.
It is easier to use it at your local machine.
Compile with:
  cd [your checkout path]/trunk
  doxygen documentation/config.dox
  cd documentation/latex
  make
Open (on linux):
  firefox documentation/html/index.html
  gnome-open latex/refman.pdf
Open (on Mac):
  open documentation/html/index.html 
  open latex/refman.pdf

Note that the Doxygen needs to be installed. On MacOS type:
  brew install doxygen  
